On 30.01.2012 19:24 (UTC+1), Michael Lawrence wrote:
> Well, I would have assumed that the Qt module for cmake would give me
> the correct flags for building a QtOpenGL program.  I will look into
> this. In the meantime, you might have to do something like put the GL
> headers into /usr/include or some other hack.

I am afraid I only have very poor programming skills.

One possibility could be that /usr/local/include/qt4/QtOpenGL/qgl.h does
not find gl.h and glu.h in this context? This is not a linux
environment, but a BSD (FreeBSD) one. Is there any chance to test this?

BTW, I tried with linking GL/gl.h and GL/glu.h into /usr/local/include.

Thanks for answering,
Rainer

